<SubSection title="Getting Started" id="Getting Started">
<p>3D printer technology is rapidly evolving. This means the material and size scale you can print at is constantly expanding. This page aims to provide tips and tricks for getting started with 3D printing to help you create models of engineering designs.</p>
</SubSection>
<SubSection title="Best Practices" id="Best Practices">
<p>Filleting corners will reduce printer head pausing that results in cooling and bed lift. Rounded (or filleted) corners keep the printer head moving and reduce temperature variations and reduce printed part warping.</p>
</SubSection>
